ld og annoncerelevans. Maksimal opbevaringstid : 2 år Type : HTTP Cookie _ga_# Benyttes til at indsamle data om brugerens platform (PC, tablet el. mobil) og præferencer - Disse data benyttes af Google Analytics til at optimere hjemmesidens indhold og annoncerelevans. Maksimal opbevaringstid : 2 år Type : HTTP Cookie Hotjar 5 Få mere at vide om denne udbyder _hjSession_# Indsamler statistik om den besøgendes besøg på hjemmesiden såsom antallet af besøg, den gennemsnitlige tid på hjemmesiden og hvilke sider der er læst. Maksimal opbevaringstid : 1 dag Type : HTTP Cookie _hjSessionUser_# Indsamler statistik om den besøgendes besøg på hjemmesiden såsom antallet af besøg, den gennemsnitlige tid på hjemmesiden og hvilke sider der er læst. Maksimal opbevaringstid : 1 år Type : HTTP Cookie _hjTLDTest Registrerer data af statistisk karakter over flere brugeres navigation på hjemmesiden. Benyttes til intern analyse og statistik. Maksimal opbevaringstid : Session Type : HTTP Cookie hjActiveViewportIds Denne cookie bruges kun under det aktuelle besøg; her indsamles der udelukkende ikke-personlig information omkring, hvilke undersider der besøges. Denne information bruges af hjemmesiden til at optimere deres hjemmeside og undersider. Maksimal opbevaringstid : Permanent Type : Lokalt HTML-lager hjViewportId Lagrer brugerens skærmstørrelse for at tilpasse størrelsen af billeder på hjemmesiden. Maksimal opbevaringstid : Session Type : Lokalt HTML-lager Siteimprove 2 Få mere at vide om denne udbyder nmstat Denne cookie bruges kun under det aktuelle besøg; her indsamles der udelukkende ikke-personlig information omkring, hvilke undersider der besøges. Denne information bruges af hjemmesiden til at optimere deres hjemmeside og undersider. Maksimal opbevaringstid : 1000 dage Type : HTTP Cookie image.aspx Registrerer data af statistisk karakter over flere brugeres navigation på hjemmesiden. Benyttes til intern analyse og statistik. Maksimal opbevaringstid : Session Type : Pixel Tracker Sleeknote 2 Få mere at vide om denne udbyder sn_global_countdown_last_reset_timestamp Sætter et tidsstempel for hvornår den besøgende tilgik hjemmesiden. Benyttes til analytiske formål. Maksimal opbevaringstid : Permanent Type : Lokalt HTML-lager SNS Sætter et unikt ID for det aktuelle besøg. Dette tillader hjemmesiden at skelne individuelle besøg fra hinanden,  hvilket benyttes til intern statistik og analyse. Maksimal opbevaringstid : Session Type : HTTP Cookie Vimeo 2 Få mere at vide om denne udbyder orionV3#identity Benyttes til indsamling data omhandlende brugerens interaktion med indlejret indhold. Maksimal opbevaringstid : Permanent Type : IndexedDB vuid Indsamler data om brugerens besøg på hjemmesiden såsom hvilke sider der er læst. Maksimal opbevaringstid : 2 år Type : HTTP Cookie Marketing 16 Marketing cookies bruges til at spore brugere på tværs af websites. Hensigten er at vise annoncer, der er relevante og engagerende for den enkelte bruger, og dermed mere værdifulde for udgivere og tredjeparts-annoncører. Meta Platforms, Inc. 4 Få mere at vide om denne udbyder _fbp Anvendes af Facebook til at levere forskellige reklame-tjenester, herunder realtids-bud fra tredjeparts-annoncører. Maksimal opbevaringstid : 3 mdr. Type : HTTP Cookie lastExternalReferrer Identificere hvordan brugeren har tilgået siden ved at registrere hvilken hjemmeside brugeren kommer fra. Maksimal opbevaringstid : Permanent Type : Lokalt HTML-lager lastExternalReferrerTime Identificere hvordan brugeren har tilgået siden ved at registrere hvilken hjemmeside brugeren kommer fra. Maksimal opbevaringstid : Permanent Type : Lokalt HTML-lager log/error Benyttes til at identificere of logge potentielle fejl i forbindelse med bruger tracking. Maksimal opbevaringstid : Session Type : Pixel Tracker Google 5 Få mere at vide om denne udbyder Nogle af de data, der indsamles af denne udbyder, er til personalisering og måling af reklameeffektivitet. Udbyderen kan bruge IP-adresserne til måling og personalisering af annoncer. _gcl_au Benyttes til at måle effektiviteten af hjemmesiden marketing-indsats, ved at måle på konversionsraten på hjemmesidens annoncer på tværs af hjemmesider. Maksimal opbevaringstid : 3 mdr. Type : HTTP Cookie IDE Anvendes af Google DoubleClick til at registrere og rapportere om hjemmesidebrugerens handlinger efter at have set eller klikket på en af annoncørens annoncer. Formålet er at måle effekten af en annonce samt at målrette annoncer til brugeren. Maksimal opbevaringstid : 400 dage Type : HTTP Cookie pagead/1p-user-list/# Indsamler data om brugerens interesse i specifikke produkter eller begivenheder på tværs af hjemmesider. Indsamler også data om brugerens navigation imellem hjemmesider. Benyttes til at optimere samt måle på annoncernes effektivitet. Benyttes yderligere til at facilitere betaling af henvisnings-gebyrer imellem hjemmesider. Maksimal opbevaringstid : Session Type : Pixel Tracker ccm/conversion/1062015234/ Afventer Maksimal opbevaringstid : Session Type : Pixel Tracker _gcl_ls Registrerer responsraten mellem brugeren og hjemmesidens pop-up annoncer - Dette benyttes til at optimere annoncernes relevans på hjemmesiden. Maksimal opbevaringstid : Permanent Type : Lokalt HTML-lager Sleeknote 3 Få mere at vide om denne udbyder _sn_a Implementerer pop-up annoncer på hjemmesiden. Maksimal opbevaringstid : 1 år Type : HTTP Cookie _sn_m Implementerer pop-up annoncer på hjemmesiden. Maksimal opbevaringstid : 1 år Type : HTTP Cookie _sn_n Implementerer pop-up annoncer på hjemmesiden. Maksimal opbevaringstid : 1 år Type : HTTP Cookie Vimeo 4 Få mere at vide om denne udbyder picox#events Benyttes til indsamling data omhandlende brugerens interaktion med indlejret indhold. Maksimal opbevaringstid : Permanent Type : IndexedDB LOCAL_STORAGE_ID_PICOX_ID Benyttes til indsamling data omhandlende brugerens interaktion med indlejret indhold. Maksimal opbevaringstid : Permanent Type : Lokalt HTML-lager LOCAL_STORAGE_ID_VIMEO_PLAYER Benyttes til indsamling data omhandlende brugerens interaktion med indlejret indhold. Maksimal opbevaringstid : Permanent Type : Lokalt HTML-lager PLAYER_PICOX_SAMPLING_SEED Benyttes til indsamling data omhandlende brugerens interaktion med indlejret indhold. Maksimal opbevaringstid : Permanent Type : Lokalt HTML-lager Uklassificeret 1 Uklassificerede cookies er cookies, som vi er i færd med at klassificere sammen med udbyderne af de enkelte cookies. Sleeknote 1 Få mere at vide om denne udbyder l:https://# Afventer Maksimal opbevaringstid : 1 år Type : HTTP Cookie Samtykke på tværs af domæner [#BULK_CONSENT_DOMAINS_COUNT#] [#BULK_CONSENT_TITLE#] Liste over domæner, dit samtykke gælder for: [#BULK_CONSENT_DOMAINS#] Cookiedeklarationen er sidst opdateret d. 8/23/26 af Cookiebot [#IABV2_TITLE#] [#IABV2_BODY_INTRO#] [#IABV2_BODY_LEGITIMATE_INTEREST_INTRO#] [#IABV2_BODY_PREFERENCE_INTRO#] [#IABV2_LABEL_PURPOSES#] [#IABV2_BODY_PURPOSES_INTRO#] [#IABV2_BODY_PURPOSES#] [#IABV2_LABEL_FEATURES#] [#IABV2_BODY_FEATURES_INTRO#] [#IABV2_BODY_FEATURES#] [#IABV2_LABEL_PARTNERS#] [#IABV2_BODY_PARTNERS_INTRO#] [#IABV2_BODY_PARTNERS#] Om CBS behandler oplysninger om dig i overenstemmelse med persondatalovgivningen. Læs mere om behandlingen om persondata i vores privatlivspolitik. Hvis du på noget tidspunkt ønsker ændre dit samtykke, så kan du gøre det på samme side. Cookies er små tekstfiler, som kan bruges af websteder til at gøre en brugers oplevelse mere effektiv. Loven fastslår, at vi kan gemme cookies på din enhed, hvis de er strengt nødvendige for at sikre leveringen af den tjeneste, du udtrykkeligt har anmodet om at bruge. For alle andre typer cookies skal vi indhente dit samtykke. Dette websted bruger forskellige typer af cookies. Nogle cookies sættes af tredjeparts tjenester, der vises på vores sider. Du kan til enhver tid ændre eller tilbagetrække dit samtykke fra Cookiedeklarationen på vores hjemmeside. Få mere at vide om, hvem vi er, hvordan du kan kontakte os, og hvordan vi behandler persondata i vores Privatlivspolitik. Angiv venligst dit samtykke-ID og -dato, når du kontakter os angående dit samtykke. Sælg eller del ikke mine personlige oplysninger Tillad alle cookies Tilpas Tillad valgte Kun nødvendige cookies Skip to main content Close Study programmes Study programmes Bachelor programmes Bachelor programmes How to choose Compare bachelor programmes Application and admission Study start Master programmes and career options Contact Master programmes Master programmes Choose your master programme Compare master programmes Application and admission Study Start Part-time master CEMS - Ma­ster in In­ter­na­tio­nal Ma­na­ge­ment (MIM) Double Degree Contact Courses Courses Courses at bachelor level Courses at master level Minors Credit transfer students Single course students Supplementary courses for master admission Registration and deadlines Student life Student life Teaching and working methods Exams Student job and career In need of special support? Summer University Summer University Application and deadlines Bachelor courses at Summer University Master courses at Summer University Course preparation Exams International Summer University Students International students International students International full-degree students Exchange students Exchange students Course application Undergraduate courses Graduate courses Housing Freemover Executive education Executive education HD-uddannelser HD-uddannelser Alle HD-Uddannelser Kurser Tilmelding og betaling Adgangskrav For virksomheder Kontakt Executive Master Programmes Executive Master Programmes Master of Business Development Master of Management Development Master of Public Governance Master i Skat MBA Programmes MBA Programmes Full-time MBA Executive MBA Executive MBA in Shipping and Logistics Executive Certificates MBA Alumni Contact CBS Executive Upgrade Courses Events Research Research Departments Centres and Units Research Profile PhD at CBS Library Library Use the library Use the library Lending rules Opening hours Print, scan and copy Search the library Search the library Online resources How to search using keywords How to search using references How to search using AI Bibliographies and citations Contact the library About CBS About CBS Organisation Organisation For companies For alumni For alumni Education documentation Previously offered programmes Grade Point Average rankings External examiner Profile Profile Strategy Strategy Geopolitics Lifelong Learning Di­git­al­isa­tion and AI Reports and key figures Educational quality International collaboration International collaboration Erasmus Job and Career Job and Career Vacant positions Employees at CBS International Employees External lecturer News from CBS Contact CBS Contact CBS Press Press Ekspertlister Close Explore our knowledge Search Dansk Da English En Search Menu Home Study programmes Student life Student job and career Stu­dent job and ca­reer Learn more about your options for a student job alongside your studies. Read about where CBS students work, how to find a student job and how to balance your studies with work. Stu­dent job Student jobs alongside your studies Most CBS students have a student job and work an average of around 15 hours per week alongside their studies. A student job is not only a source of extra income. It is also a great way to gain experience, develop skills and build a professional network that can make the transition to your first full-time job easier. Where do CBS students work? CBS is located in the heart of Copenhagen, close to large international companies, start-ups, consultancy firms, banks, organisations and public institutions. This provides good opportunities for student jobs across a wide range of industries and positions. Some students work in areas related to what they study, such as analysis, finance or marketing, while others work in areas such as the service sector, retail or customer service. A student job can take many forms In a study-relevant student job, you work with what you learn in your programme and gain the opportunity to apply theory in practice. This may include tasks such as data analysis, preparing reports and presentations, assisting with accounting tasks, planning campaigns, coordinating projects or contributing to the development of new business initiatives. Other types of student jobs, for example service jobs in shops, restaurants or bars, can also help you develop valuable skills such as teamwork, responsibility and customer interaction and in some cases leadership. These skills are also in demand by many employers. Work­ing while study­ing at CBS Hear Onel, Alvaro and Ailada tell about their student job and experiences with working in Denmark. You must accept preference cookies to view this video. The perfect student job from the start? When you find a study-relevant student job often depends on where you are in your studies: Bachelor students Very few students have a study-relevant student job from the beginning. For many, the start of their studies is about settling in, building relationships and developing good study habits. Typically, students find a study-relevant student job later in their bachelor or master programme. Some students continue in the job they had during their gap year, while others choose not to work at the beginning in order to focus on learning how to be a student. Master students For master students, a student job often plays a bigger role in strengthening their job opportunities after graduation. Some continue in the student job they had during their bachelor programme, while others change direction or work in a more specialised role within their field of study. For many, a student job also becomes a pathway into the labour market, and some continue in a permanent position with the same employer. A study-relevant student job can therefore serve as a springboard to your first full-time job. Alternative ways to gain experience A student job is far from the only way to gain experience during your studies. Voluntary work, internships or projects and assignments carried out in collaboration with a company are all good ways to gain experience and build a network that can also open doors to your future working life. At the same time, your education at CBS provides a solid academic foundation in itself, which you can build on through different types of experience along the way. Balancing studies and work It is important that a student job fits in with your studies and everyday life. Most employers are used to hiring students and take teaching schedules and exam periods into account. Many students choose to prioritise a student job because it provides experience and skills that are highly valued by employers. At the same time, it is important to create balance in your daily life so there is room for studies, work and leisure. “A relevant student job is not just a professional stepping stone into working life – it’s also a chance to explore your interests and build confidence. The most important thing is that you’re genuinely interested and remember that you often can do more than you think. You don’t have to be perfect.” Frank Career counsellor EX­PER­I­ENCE MAT­TERS MORE THAN GRADES 75% of Danish companies place emphasis on relevant experience when hiring newly graduated candidates, while only 2% prioritise high grades (Recruitment Analysis 2023, Ballisager). This does not mean that grades are unimportant and you should of course prioritise your studies – but it shows that relevant work experience helps strengthen your skills and makes you more attractive in the labour market. Ca­reer activ­it­ies and op­por­tun­it­ies at CBS As a CBS student, you can take part in a range of career events and opportunities designed to help you find a student job and prepare for the labour market. Find a stu­dent job on CBS’ job portal CBS has its own job portal called CBS CareerGate . As a student, you can find: Relevant student jobs Projects in collaboration with companies Internships Graduate programmes Full-time jobs Exciting company events Please note that you must be a CBS student to access CareerGate. Take part in ca­reer events You can take part in a range of career events held on campus, such as: Career Fair Consulting event Graduate event Career seminars Get a ment­or You can be matched with a career mentor from the business community. The mentors are CBS alumni who now work in companies and organisations in Denmark and abroad. They are ready to support you and your career development. Get ca­reer coun­sel­ing As a CBS student or recent graduate, you can receive free career counseling on all aspects of your career. This includes feedback on your CV and application, help getting started, as well as skills assessment and career clarification. Find tools for your job search You will get access to practical tools and guidance to help you search for and find a student job. This includes tools on how to create a targeted CV, write a strong application, tips for LinkedIn and how to prepare for job interviews and different types of tests. For in­ter­na­tion­al stu­dents Student jobs in Denmark Many students at CBS have a student job alongside their studies. A student job can be a valuable way to gain experience, build a network and gain insight into how workplaces function in Denmark. However, as an international student, it may take time to find a student job. Some positions require Danish, and competition for English-speaking roles can be high. Many international students start in broader roles, such as service or customer-facing jobs, and gradually move towards positions that are more closely related to their field of study. If you are interested in working in Denmark after graduation, gaining relevant experience during your studies can be especially valuable. A student job can help you build a professional network and better understand the Danish job market, making the transition from studies to working life smoother and quicker. The Danish language While English is used in many workplaces, learning Danish can improve your opportunities, both during and after your studies. See your options for learning Danish . Working in Denmark Denmark offers a work environment that many international students find attractive. Workplaces are often characterised by flat hierarchies, trust and open communication, as well as a strong focus on equality and work-life balance. Even in student jobs, you are often given responsibility and the opportunity to contribute to real tasks, which can be valuable when building experience during your studies. Work permit for international students As an international student, you will most likely need a work permit to work alongside your studies. Read more about work permits and working in Denmark Ca­reer sup­port and pro­grammes In addition to CBS’ own career activities, our external partners offer programmes specifically designed for international students who wish to build a career in Denmark. These programmes are free of charge for CBS students. Explore your options. Great­er Copen­ha­gen Ca­reer Pro­gramme The Greater Copenhagen Career Programme is a 7‑month mentoring and networking programme that prepares you for a career in Denmark. It is offered to international bachelor’s and master’s students in the Greater Copenhagen area. The programme provides you with: Knowledge of how to structure your CV, job application, and LinkedIn profile Training in presenting yourself professionally and using your network A personal career mentor Read more about Greater Copenhagen Career Programme Ca­reer Kick Start Career Kick Start is a short course designed to help you find a student job or an internship in Denmark. It is offered to international bachelor’s and master’s students in their first year of study. What you’ll get: Learn how to structure your CV, job application, and LinkedIn profile Learn how to approach companies and present yourself professionally Learn how to use your network and take part in company activities Read more about Career Kick Start Dream­ing of be­com­ing an en­tre­pren­eur? You can get support to build your own startup through Copenhagen School of Entrepreneurship (CSE). At CSE, you become part of an active entrepreneurial community with workshops, mentoring, office space, and networking opportunities - so you can work on your idea alongside your studies. Read more about Copenhagen School of Entrepreneurship Read more about stu­dent life Learn more about what it is like to be a stu­dent at CBS. You can e.g. read about pro­gramme struc­ture, teach­ing activ­it­ies, exam formats, or the so­cial life on cam­pus. Stu­dent life at CBS Get a glimpse of student life at CBS. Here, you can explore what a typical day of teaching and exams looks like. You can learn how our programmes are… Read more Teach­ing and work­ing meth­ods At CBS you will have both lectures and exercise classes. You should also expect to spend time on preparing for classes and exams both individually and in… Read more Ex­ams At CBS you conclude all courses with an exam. Along the way in your programme you may encounter different exam formats such as written on-site exams , written… Read more In need of spe­cial sup­port? Do you have a disability such as dyslexia, anxiety, autism, ADHD, long-term effects following a concussion or another physical, mental or neurological… Read more We transform society with business. Study programmes Executive education Research Library About CBS Copenhagen Business School Solbjerg Plads 3 2000\n            \n                          Frederiksberg CVR number: 19596915 EAN number: 5798009814821 Contact us and visit campus Press All news For companies Opens in a new tab Opens in a new tab Opens in a new tab Copyright © CBS 2026 Data pro­tec­tion at CBS Accessibility statement Whistleblower scheme"
    },
