 kontakte os, og hvordan vi behandler persondata i vores Privatlivspolitik. Angiv venligst dit samtykke-ID og -dato, når du kontakter os angående dit samtykke. Sælg eller del ikke mine personlige oplysninger Tillad alle cookies Tilpas Tillad valgte Kun nødvendige cookies Skip to main content Close Study programmes Study programmes Bachelor programmes Bachelor programmes How to choose Compare bachelor programmes Application and admission Study start Master programmes and career options Contact Master programmes Master programmes Choose your master programme Compare master programmes Application and admission Study Start Part-time master CEMS - Ma­ster in In­ter­na­tio­nal Ma­na­ge­ment (MIM) Double Degree Contact Courses Courses Courses at bachelor level Courses at master level Minors Credit transfer students Single course students Supplementary courses for master admission Registration and deadlines Student life Student life Teaching and working methods Exams Student job and career In need of special support? Summer University Summer University Application and deadlines Bachelor courses at Summer University Master courses at Summer University Course preparation Exams International Summer University Students International students International students International full-degree students Exchange students Exchange students Course application Undergraduate courses Graduate courses Housing Freemover Executive education Executive education HD-uddannelser HD-uddannelser Alle HD-Uddannelser Kurser Tilmelding og betaling Adgangskrav For virksomheder Kontakt Executive Master Programmes Executive Master Programmes Master of Business Development Master of Management Development Master of Public Governance Master i Skat MBA Programmes MBA Programmes Full-time MBA Executive MBA Executive MBA in Shipping and Logistics Executive Certificates MBA Alumni Contact CBS Executive Upgrade Courses Events Research Research Departments Centres and Units Research Profile PhD at CBS Library Library Use the library Use the library Lending rules Opening hours Print, scan and copy Search the library Search the library Online resources How to search using keywords How to search using references How to search using AI Bibliographies and citations Contact the library About CBS About CBS Organisation Organisation For companies For alumni For alumni Education documentation Previously offered programmes Grade Point Average rankings External examiner Profile Profile Strategy Strategy Geopolitics Lifelong Learning Di­git­al­isa­tion and AI Reports and key figures Educational quality International collaboration International collaboration Erasmus Job and Career Job and Career Vacant positions Employees at CBS International Employees External lecturer News from CBS Contact CBS Contact CBS Press Press Ekspertlister Close Explore our knowledge Search Dansk Da English En Search Menu Home About CBS Job and Career Vacant positions Head of Department of Finance, Copenhagen Business School Head of De­part­ment of Fin­ance, Copen­ha­gen Busi­ness School Apply now Unit Copenhagen Business School Application deadline 20 September 2026 Copenhagen Business School (CBS) invites applications for the position of Head of Department of Finance (FI) , starting 1 January 2027. This is a unique opportunity to lead one of Europe’s leading academic environments in finance and contribute to CBS’ ambition to transform society with business. About the position As Head of Department (HoD), you are responsible for the strategic, academic and organisational leadership of FI. Working closely with faculty and staff, with CBS Senior Management and with HoD colleagues across CBS, you play a central role in shaping the department’s academic profile, supporting a strong and inclusive working environment, and contributing to CBS’ overall strategic development. FI is one of Europe’s leading research environments in finance, with internationally recognised research in financial economics, register-data research, statistics and machine learning. The department brings together 50 faculty members, 15 PhD students, 11 administrative staff and around 200 external lecturers and plays a central role in research, education and societal engagement at CBS. As HoD you will build on the department’s strong international position, support continued research excellence, develop talent and enhance the department’s long-term organisational resilience, capacity and impact. Your key responsibilities Provide strategic and academic leadership of FI in alignment with CBS’ strategy “ We transform Society with Business” Fostering research excellence, talent development and high-quality research-based teaching Attracting, developing and supporting academic and administrative colleagues, with attention to diversity, inclusion and professional growth Supporting external funding opportunities and building solid partnerships with societal stakeholders Promoting a healthy, collaborative and inclusive work environment We are looking for We are looking for an internationally recognised researcher with a strong research profile in finance and demonstrated leadership skills in research and/or education. You are expected to be qualified at minimum Associate Professor level or equivalent. You are committed to maintaining and further developing a world-class environment in finance and demonstrates: Documented experience in research and educational leadership Ability to lead complex organisations, budgets and resources Effective communication skills, an international outlook and an interest in research and societal impact Commitment to diversity, equity and inclusion in academic leadership A visible and approachable leadership style that supports collaboration, trust and well-being Motivation for leadership and for continuing to develop in the leadership role Terms of employment Time-limited position (typically 6 years, with possible extension) The employment follows the Danish collective agreement for academics, in line with the Danish University Act and CBS’ bylaws The salary consists of a fixed base salary, and supplementary allowances upon negotiation An agreement to return to a scientific position at the Department upon expiry of employment as HoD is possible provided that the individual’s research and scholarly contributions fall within those of the Department The HoD reports to Dean of Research, Innovation and Societal Impact Morten Frederiksen Application process Application deadline: 20 September 2026 Expected start date: 1 January 2027 Applications must be submitted via CBS’ electronic recruitment system, including CV, documentation of research and teaching qualifications, evidence of leadership experience, and a vision statement for the department. Want to know more? Please consult the full Job and Person Profile for Head of Department of Finance and The CBS Leadership Code before applying, available here: Job and Person Profile and Lead ership Code . For questions, please contact President Peter Mølgaard at rektor@cbs.dk or HR-Partner Marianne Krabbe at makr.hr@cbs.dk . All inquiries will be treated confidentially. We encourage all interested candidates to apply – even if you do not meet every listed criterion. A strong research background and leadership potential are essential. WE TRANSFORM SOCIETY WITH BUSINESS CBS is a globally recognised business school with deep roots in the Nordic socio-economic model. Our faculty has a broad focus on societal challenges, and we have earned a reputation for high-quality disciplinary and interdisciplinary research and education. We are located at Frederiksberg and have approximately 20,000 full and part-time students, 800 full-time faculty members, 200 PhD students and 700 administrative staff, and a full portfolio of bachelor, master, MBA/EMBA, PhD and executive programmes taught in English and Danish. Our global profile carries the obligation to address critical challenges in our research and to develop the transformational capabilities of students, graduates and business leaders via our educational activities and opportunities for lifelong learning. Complex challenges call for joint action, and therefore our strategy focuses on strengthening current and starting new partnerships with other sciences, the business community, authorities and civil society. CBS is working continuously on becoming a diverse and inclusive organisation, and we encourage all regardless of gender identity and expression, ethnicity, religious beliefs, LGBT+ status, cultural background etc. to apply. Reach out to us if you need assistance in the application or recruitment process, if there is something we should know, or if as a person with disability you wish to make use of your preferential access. We transform society with business. Study programmes Executive education Research Library About CBS Copenhagen Business School Solbjerg Plads 3 2000\n            \n                          Frederiksberg CVR number: 19596915 EAN number: 5798009814821 Contact us and visit campus Press All news For companies Opens in a new tab Opens in a new tab Opens in a new tab Copyright © CBS 2026 Data pro­tec­tion at CBS Accessibility statement Whistleblower scheme"
    },
